==============================================================================
slide_selftest.py -- primitive self-tests and false controls
==============================================================================

-- imported primitive self-tests (mjm + ptm) --
  [PASS] orientR ccw > 0
  [PASS] orientR cw  < 0
  [PASS] orientR collinear = 0
  [PASS] orientR matches the Lean formula on a sample
  [PASS] on_closed at start endpoint
  [PASS] on_closed at end endpoint
  [PASS] on_closed at interior point
  [PASS] on_closed rejects the collinear extension
  [PASS] on_closed rejects an off-line point
  [PASS] proper_cross on a genuine X
  [PASS] proper_cross FALSE at a shared endpoint (touching, not crossing)
  [PASS] proper_cross FALSE for a T-touch
  [PASS] SimpleClosed accepts a convex heptagon
  [PASS] SimpleClosed ACCEPTS three collinear vertices (deliberate)
  [PASS] SimpleClosed REJECTS a self-crossing heptagon
  [PASS] SimpleClosed REJECTS an adjacent-side backtrack (conjunct 3)
  [PASS] SimpleClosed REJECTS a repeated vertex (conjunct 1)
  [PASS] moveV changes exactly one vertex
  [PASS] moveV moves it by exactly e*E
  [PASS] moveV with e=0 is the identity
  [PASS] test square-ish P is simple
  [PASS] coincSet finds the translate's shared vertices
  [PASS] designed X-pair: both simple
  [PASS] designed X-pair: exactly one coincidence
  [PASS] a coincidence puts 2 entries in segDeg and 2 in segDegP
  [PASS] finite_intersection says NO on an overlapping collinear pair
  [PASS] finite_intersection says YES on a transversal pair
  -- new degPts tests --
  [PASS] crescent witness: degPts has exactly 3 points
  [PASS] crescent witness: degPts is exactly {(0,0),(3,8),(8,3)}
  [PASS] crescent witness: exactly one coincidence, at (0,0)
  [PASS] the coincidence occupies 4 slots in segDeg+segDegP but 1 point in degPts
  [PASS] crescent witness: |segDeg|+|segDegP| = 6 while |degPts| = 3
  [PASS] crescent witness: M_seg = 7, M_pt = 4
  [PASS] degPts agrees with the direct definition (crescent)
  [PASS] disjoint-vertex translate: degPts empty, agrees with direct
  [PASS] T-touch fixture is simple and has NO coincidence
  [PASS] T-touch: degPts agrees with the direct definition
  [PASS] T-touch: Q[0]=(3,0) strictly inside a P-side is exactly one degPt
  [PASS] degPts is symmetric in (P,Q)
  [PASS] moveV changes exactly one vertex (re-checked here)
  [PASS] the moved pair has strictly fewer coincidences
  [PASS] degPts agrees with the direct definition on 120 random pairs (and their moves)

-- slide-specific self-tests --
  [PASS] designed pair simple
  [PASS] designed pair has the coincidence P[0]=Q[0]
  [PASS] slide A direction is P[v]-P[v+1]
  [PASS] slide B direction is P[v]-P[v-1]
  [PASS] slide changes exactly one P vertex
  [PASS] slide A: old side v is contained in the NEW side v (every e>0)
  [PASS] slide A: the OLD apex lies on the new side v
  [PASS] degPts agrees with the direct definition
  [PASS] degPts counts the coincidence exactly ONCE
  [PASS] ...while segDeg+segDegP charge it FOUR times
  [PASS] suppP of a P-vertex is its two incident sides
  [PASS] suppP of a side midpoint is that one side
  [PASS] SimpleClosed accepts a straight pass-through at P[1]
  [PASS] ...and P[1] is strictly between P[0] and P[2]
  [PASS] SimpleClosed REJECTS the collinear backtrack (apex not in the middle)

-- DELIBERATELY FALSE CONTROLS (these MUST fail) --
  control corpus: 210 instances, hardM=30 hardN=60 hardP=60 plain=60
  FALSE CONTROL 1  'slide A admissible at e=0'  : holds 0/210  -> 210 failures
  FALSE CONTROL 2  'M_pt strictly increases'    : holds 92/203  -> 111 failures
  FALSE CONTROL 3  'no degPt is ever lost'      : holds 177/203  -> 26 failures
  (reference, expected TRUE) 'M_pt non-decreasing': holds 187/203
  [PASS] false control 1 does fail
  [PASS] false control 2 does fail
  [PASS] harness is sensitive: at least one degPt loss somewhere

SELFTEST OK

